2. Third-Party Dependencies and Ultralytics AGPL Gate
------------------------------------------------------
AI Vision Trainer interfaces with third-party machine learning frameworks,
most notably Ultralytics YOLO (including YOLO11 and YOLO26 model architectures).

IMPORTANT NOTICE REGARDING ULTRALYTICS LICENSING:
- Ultralytics YOLO software is published by Ultralytics LLC under the
  GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0) for open source use.
- Under AGPL-3.0, if you modify or run Ultralytics software over a network,
  you may be obligated to make your complete corresponding source code available.
- For commercial, proprietary, or closed-source deployments where AGPL-3.0
  compliance is not acceptable, organizations MUST acquire an Ultralytics
  Commercial License directly from Ultralytics LLC (https://www.ultralytics.com/license).
- AI Vision Trainer isolates model adapter execution to ensure explicit boundaries,
  but users and organizations deploying this software are solely responsible for
  compliance with upstream model and dataset licenses.

3. Dataset and Pretrained Weight Licensing
------------------------------------------
Pretrained model checkpoints (e.g., weights downloaded from public repositories
such as COCO, Objects365, or Ultralytics release assets) and public datasets are
governed by their respective original publisher licenses. Users must verify
that any dataset used for training complies with their intended commercial or
academic usage terms.
